---
import Contents from "../../editorial/Contents.astro";
import Band from "../../editorial/Band.astro";

const sections = [
	{ n: "02", title: "The engine", blurb: "What the 22R-E actually is and where it came from.", href: "#engine-history" },
	{ n: "03", title: "What breaks", blurb: "What tends to fail on a 22RE, from hundreds of real forum threads.", href: "#failure-points" },
	{ n: "04", title: "The market", blurb: "What this era of Toyota truck has actually sold for.", href: "#market-value" },
	{ n: "05", title: "Hawaii", blurb: "Why this truck and this brand mean something specific here.", href: "#hawaii-culture" },
];
---

<section id="the-data">
	<Band tone="ink" cx={120} cy={560} innerClass="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 md:grid-cols-12">
		<div class="md:col-span-5">
			<p class="font-mono inline-block -rotate-1 bg-spot px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] uppercase text-black">Part two: the data</p>
			<p class="font-display mt-6 text-xl font-semibold leading-snug md:text-2xl">
				That's the truck's story. I'm also the kind of person who wants to actually understand what I'm getting into,
				not just feel good about it.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base font-medium leading-relaxed">
				So alongside the wrenching, here's what I dug into: what the engine actually is and where it came from. What
				actually tends to break on a 22RE, pulled from hundreds of real forum threads. What the market for this era of
				Toyota trucks has actually looked like. And why, beyond my own family's story, this truck and this brand mean
				something specific in Hawaii.
			</p>
		</div>
		<Contents items={sections} class="md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7" />
	</Band>
</section>
